{"paper": "SSC-DelhiPoliceConstable-03-Dec-2023-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 15, "tagged_count": 15, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1000", "added": false}, {"text": "10000", "added": false}, {"text": "100", "added": false}, {"text": "5000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "Find the greatest common divisor of 65, 75 and 90.", "options": [{"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "13", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "The marked price of a commodity was ₹3,675. The seller offered a discount of 12% on its sale and incurred a loss of 2% as a consequence. What was the cost price (in ₹) of the commodity?", "options": [{"text": "3275", "added": false}, {"text": "3300", "added": false}, {"text": "3280", "added": false}, {"text": "3350", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "25", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "If Basket A has 9 apples and 12 bananas, Basket B has 10 apples and 15 bananas, and Basket C has 8 apples and 16 bananas, then the ratios of apples and bananas in ____________.", "options": [{"text": "Basket A < Basket C", "added": false}, {"text": "Basket A < Basket B", "added": false}, {"text": "Basket A = Basket C", "added": false}, {"text": "Basket A > Basket B", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "In how much time (in years) will a sum of ₹3,125 become ₹3,515.20 at 8% per annum, compounded half-yearly?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "compounding-frequency", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "3 men and 4 women can do a work in 7 days, whereas 2 men and 1 woman can do it in 14 days. 7 women will complete the same work in:", "options": [{"text": "8 days", "added": false}, {"text": "10 days", "added": false}, {"text": "12 days", "added": false}, {"text": "9 days", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "group-work", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "For reaching at a dance class, Neelam walks at 5 km/h and reaches late by 10 min. If she increases her speed by 1 km/h, then she reaches 15 min early. Find the distance she travelled from her house to her destination.", "options": [{"text": "10.5 km", "added": false}, {"text": "12.5 km", "added": false}, {"text": "10 km", "added": false}, {"text": "5.5 km", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "early-late", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "If the cost price and selling price of an article are in the ratio of 13 : 17, then the percentage profit is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "In an election, there were two candidates Ram and Soham. The total number of voters in this constituency was 85800 and 80% of the total votes were polled. If 65% of the polled votes were cast in favour of Soham, how many votes were received by Ram?", "options": [{"text": "38038", "added": false}, {"text": "34034", "added": false}, {"text": "26026", "added": false}, {"text": "24024", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "Shashi sold her washing machine for ₹8,000; this was 60% increase in the value. What was the original price?", "options": [{"text": "₹6,200", "added": false}, {"text": "₹5,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹5,800", "added": false}, {"text": "₹5,400", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "Find the average of all prime numbers between 15 and 30.", "options": [{"text": "23", "added": false}, {"text": "25", "added": false}, {"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "22", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "Two banks, A and B, offered loans at rates 5.5% and 6.5% per annum, respectively. Ramesh borrowed an amount of ₹3,00,000 from each bank. The positive difference between the amounts of simple interest paid to the two banks by Ramesh after 2 years will be:", "options": [{"text": "₹2,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹4,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹8,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹6,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "190", "added": false}, {"text": "174", "added": false}, {"text": "192", "added": false}, {"text": "188", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}]}